{%- comment -%}
  Product card without nested interactive controls
  WCAG 4.1.2 Name Role Value, 2.4.4 Link Purpose, 1.1.1 Non-text Content

  Usage:  {% render 'a11y-product-card', product: product %}

  The failure this replaces:

    <a href="{{ product.url }}">
      <img src="...">
      <h3>{{ product.title }}</h3>
      <button>Quick add</button>          <-- button inside a link
    </a>

  A button inside a link is one target carrying two conflicting roles. Screen
  readers disagree about what to announce, keyboard activation is
  unpredictable, and axe reports it as nested-interactive. It is extremely
  common in product grids because wrapping the whole card in an anchor is the
  quickest way to make the entire card clickable.

  The fix is to keep the controls as siblings and make the card look clickable
  with a stretched pseudo-element on the title link. Mouse users get the whole
  card as a target. Keyboard and screen reader users get two clearly separate
  controls, each with its own name.

  The quick-add button carries hidden text naming the product, so that a
  screen reader user listing controls on a grid of twenty products does not
  hear "Quick add" twenty times with no way to tell them apart.
{%- endcomment -%}

<div class="a11y-card">
  <div class="a11y-card__media">
    {%- if product.featured_media -%}
      {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 600 | image_tag:
         loading: 'lazy',
         widths: '300, 600, 900',
         alt: product.featured_media.alt | default: product.title | escape }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <h3 class="a11y-card__title">
    <a class="a11y-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a>
  </h3>

  <p class="a11y-card__price">
    {%- comment -%}
      Price markup is decorated visually for sale items. The hidden text
      supplies the meaning that the strikethrough conveys visually, because
      a screen reader does not announce a line through a number.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
      <span class="visually-hidden">Sale price</span>
      <span class="a11y-card__price--sale">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
      <span class="visually-hidden">Regular price</span>
      <s>{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="visually-hidden">Price</span>
      {{ product.price | money }}
    {%- endif -%}
  </p>

  {%- if product.available and product.variants.size == 1 -%}
    <form method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}">
      <button type="submit" class="a11y-card__add">
        Quick add<span class="visually-hidden">, {{ product.title | escape }}</span>
      </button>
    </form>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{%- style -%}
  .a11y-card { position: relative; }

  /* The stretched link makes the whole card clickable for a pointer without
     nesting anything inside anything. Keep every other control above it in
     the stacking order so they stay independently clickable. */
  .a11y-card__link::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 1;
  }

  .a11y-card__add { position: relative; z-index: 2; }

  .a11y-card__link:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid currentColor;
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
